WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.560
Roxy ran into an empty room.

2
00:00:13.561 --> 00:00:20.924
A moment later she was Rocket Girl!

3
00:00:20.925 --> 00:00:26.420
Sometimes Roxy felt bad that her friends didn't know she was actually Rocket Girl.

4
00:00:26.421 --> 00:00:32.850
But Roxy had decided to tell her secret only to Mayor Bloom and Principal Penn.

5
00:00:32.851 --> 00:00:35.891
That way she could still have a normal life.

6
00:00:35.892 --> 00:00:38.203
Well, sort of normal.

7
00:00:38.204 --> 00:00:41.450
How many eight-year-olds had to save the world every day?

8
00:00:41.451 --> 00:00:44.342
But now was not the time to worry about that.

9
00:00:44.343 --> 00:00:47.281
Rocket Girl had a job to do!

10
00:00:47.282 --> 00:00:51.473
Roxy ran down the hall and out the front door of the school.

11
00:00:51.474 --> 00:00:53.708
"Okay," she said.

12
00:00:53.709 --> 00:00:57.275
"It's time to figure out what landed at Mr. Mann's farm."

13
00:00:57.276 --> 00:01:01.166
Then Roxy blasted into the air.

14
00:01:01.167 --> 00:01:04.332
"Look out the window!" cried Mara.

15
00:01:04.333 --> 00:01:11.810
"Rocket Girl!" said Terrell.

16
00:01:11.811 --> 00:01:15.437
Soon Roxy was at Mr. Mann's farm.

17
00:01:15.438 --> 00:01:18.322
She looked around.

18
00:01:18.323 --> 00:01:21.252
Some of the corn had been cut down.

19
00:01:21.253 --> 00:01:23.738
Roxy didn't see the spaceship though.

20
00:01:23.739 --> 00:01:26.789
Just then something moved in the cornfield.

21
00:01:26.790 --> 00:01:32.517
A figure stepped toward her.

22
00:01:32.518 --> 00:01:37.487
"Oh no!" Roxy laughed. "It's an alien detective!"

23
00:01:37.488 --> 00:01:42.694
"This is no time for making jokes," said Detective Smith with a frown.

24
00:01:42.695 --> 00:01:46.213
Detective Smith was Metro City's head detective.

25
00:01:46.214 --> 00:01:48.779
He was a very serious man. He

26
00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:51.302
never joked. "Fine,"

27
00:01:51.303 --> 00:01:55.760
said Roxy. "So what happened here? Where's

28
00:01:55.761 --> 00:01:58.090
the spaceship?" "I

29
00:01:58.091 --> 00:02:01.102
don't know," said Detective Smith. "I

30
00:02:01.103 --> 00:02:03.217
looked all over for it. I

31
00:02:03.218 --> 00:02:06.195
didn't see it anywhere." "Did

32
00:02:06.196 --> 00:02:09.688
Mr. Mann see where it went?" asked Roxy. "No,"

33
00:02:09.689 --> 00:02:12.058
said Detective Smith. "He

34
00:02:12.059 --> 00:02:14.791
got scared and ran into his house. He

35
00:02:14.792 --> 00:02:17.159
told me he hid under his bed. When

36
00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:20.267
he came back out, the spaceship was gone. So

37
00:02:20.268 --> 00:02:22.646
was the corn." "Why

38
00:02:22.647 --> 00:02:26.833
would the aliens take the corn?" Roxy wondered. She

39
00:02:26.834 --> 00:02:28.935
looked around. She

40
00:02:28.936 --> 00:02:33.171
saw a tree with a broken branch and flew over to it. "It

41
00:02:33.172 --> 00:02:37.139
looks like something crashed into this tree," thought Roxy. Nearby,

42
00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:39.825
a fence was also broken. Roxy

43
00:02:39.826 --> 00:02:42.688
looked from the tree to the fence. Then

44
00:02:42.689 --> 00:02:45.281
she looked past the fence. She

45
00:02:45.282 --> 00:02:48.866
could see a trail of damaged trees. "I

46
00:02:48.867 --> 00:02:52.660
bet the spaceship did that," thought Roxy. "But

47
00:02:52.661 --> 00:02:56.628
why didn't the spaceship fly over all the trees? And

48
00:02:56.629 --> 00:02:59.344
where did the spaceship go ?"

49
00:02:59.345 --> 00:03:02.249
Roxy flew up high to get a better view.

50
00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:05.147
The trail led straight toward . . .

51
00:03:05.148 --> 00:03:07.249
Roxy gulped.

52
00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:14.429
"Uh-oh! I know exactly where the spaceship went.

53
00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:20.515
It's headed toward downtown Metro City!"

